<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Marrakesh</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Marrakesh is a city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a> founded by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almoravid-empire">Almoravids</a> around 1070 as the capital of the Almoravid Empire. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almohad-caliphate">Almohads</a> captured it in 1147 and made it the capital of the Almohad <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">Caliphate</a>, adorning it with monuments such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/koutoubia-mosque">Koutoubia Mosque</a>. Its fall to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marinid-dynasty">Marinids</a> in 1269 ended Almohad rule.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/marrakesh.jpg" alt="Marrakesh" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Acp · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pavillon_Menarag%C3%A4rten.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
